  "body": "Design doc for #5789 (queue task 12947), extending the landed v1 writer-set projection (#5545, `pkgs/id/src/idset/{view,expand}.rs`) and the #2238 spec.\n\n**Doc:** `doc/2026-11-08T11-10-00Z_design_id_writer_sets_v2/2026-11-08T11-10-00Z_design_id_writer_sets_v2.md` (+ index line in `doc/README.md`)\n\nCovers every acceptance bullet for issue #5789:\n- **View-as-object (D1/D2):** the referenced object is a signed `idset.view` descriptor + frontier snapshot (not a bare set, not a frozen result); pinned (default — source changes do not propagate until a signed repin) vs tracking (follows the source's current set version; source removals propagate; referencing owner's exclusions always apply on top).\n- **Set algebra (D3/D4):** signed `idset.derived` objects over pinned operand references; union/intersection/difference over v1 expansions; per-author provenance paths replayable to signed originals; exclusions win at every level; cycles refused by construction (content-addressed operands) with unresolved operands reported as partial, never silently empty.\n- **Federation (D5):** remote authors named by key; resolution via #5675 remote query, sharing gated by #5672 (an entry is a request, never a grant); a set may claim membership only — unseen authors sit on the uncounted side as `named, not yet resolved` until their events are fetched and verified.\n- **Discovery v2 (D6):** views/sets/derived sets as discoverable objects; inherited uncounted-side honesty — a derived view must show what its sources excluded, attributed per source; exclusions are never laundered through composition.\n- **Abuse (§5):** attention/compute/fetch amplification valves, all numbers deferred to #2033.\n- **Open questions (§6):** purity preserved via a per-source frontier vector in the tuple; `include_history` through a chain is AND (most restrictive link governs); derived sets are signed to publish, reproducible to trust.\n- CBOR layouts, numeric caps, wire details, and sharing grammar explicitly deferred to their owning issues/slices (§7); implementation slices named in §8 for separate filing.\n\nDesign-only: no code changes, no v1 behaviour changes.\n\nRefs #5789\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796728280&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7651&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7651&signature=8f7d5370272ff4f310f01d1e5250f957d736af8fb280d2563418237e6294a53d\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7651?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
